## Discrepancy with pre-test predictions (RESOLVED)

The v0.3 firmware header commented an expected rate of **~17 Hz** based on 450 RPM head shaft measurement made 17/09/2026. Observed rate at full throttle is ~7 Hz — a factor of 2.4x lower than predicted.

**Resolution:** The observed pulse rate is now the authoritative calibration point. The pre-test geometric prediction (450 RPM * 9T * 1.630" pitch / 6.52" paddle spacing = 17 Hz) is superseded by direct measurement. One or more of the inputs (head shaft RPM measurement, sprocket tooth count, or pitch) was incorrect. Since the sensor now provides direct ground truth for paddle counting and occlusion width, reconciling the geometric model is a low-priority follow-up.

**Action:** Firmware header comment updated in v0.5 to reflect measured rate.

